as i  and i was really struck by how with just  a few small shifts in circumstance  we could be sitting on opposite sides of  the table  we were peers and that is supremely  unfair  that our situations were so different  yeah the sleepout this year obviously  has to be different  uh what's what are you going to do this  year  so this year uh it'll be a virtual event  obviously given what's going on  in the country and in the world but  we'll be sleeping out wherever we can  find a space whether that be  a backyard or a front yard or a living  room  i think that's where we're going to  sleep out tonight but the programming  will remain largely the same  just just in our little computer boxes  so the and so the spirit will be the  same as well  absolutely yeah you as i mentioned uh  congrats on another emmy nomination  uh how did you celebrate by the way yeah  uh well it's a little different right  now  um so i have i have a little pod that  i've been with  since march and i don't know we wanted  to do something  exciting and and somehow we came up with  making match s'mores otherwise known as  apartment s'mores  um you light a match and you  hold the marshmallow over it and it did  it felt special and celebratory  so are you planning to get dressed up  for the emmys themselves even though  you'll be at home  i'm definitely going to do something  special yeah i mean  i get to bring my dogs to the emmys how  often is that gonna happen  it's gonna be a fun night i was struck  by something that i read you'd said  before which is that you'd actually  lost parts because you weren't funny  enough  that must have made auditioning for mrs  maisel who's a stand-up comedian  pretty intimidating yeah  definitely it's still intimidating we're  three  four years in and it doesn't get any  less intimidating  but i think it just goes to show that we  shouldn't put ourselves in those boxes  you know for a long time i had  turned down auditions because i'd been  told for so long that 